thub.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2472) migration, [PR #2486](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2486) seam (ADR 0050) |"," | ✅ | [#2387](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2387) Ship THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES (or an SPDX SBOM) in the images and GitHub releases — [PR #2461](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2461): `scripts/check-licenses.py` gate in CI + pre-commit, `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` in both images (frontend serves `/third-party-notices`), SPDX SBOM + notices attached to the GitHub Release by a read-only tag-time job; one override (`caio`), zero violations |","-| ⬜ | [#2388](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2388) Portable install artifact: a Helm chart (ADR 0013 Phase 2) |","-| ⬜ | [#2253](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2253) docs(marketing): a walkthrough of the demo profile on the marketing page (video or annotated screenshots) |","-| ⬜ | [#1664](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/1664) docs(positioning): adopt the 'Data Quality Control Plane' framing on the marketing page + docs site |","+| ✅ | [#2388](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2388) Portable install artifact: a Helm chart (ADR 0013 Phase 2) — [PR #2505](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2505): `deploy/helm/dataq/` (migrate as a pre-install/pre-upgrade hook, no credential in values, non-root read-only pods), rendered and kubeconform-checked in CI; kind smoke is a documented manual step |","+| ✅ | [#2253](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2253) docs(marketing): a walkthrough of the demo profile on the marketing page (video or annotated screenshots) — [PR #2501](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2501): five annotated screenshots of the demo profile on the marketing page; screenshots 3 and 4 need recapturing after [#2499](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2499) and [#2502](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2502) |","+| ✅ | [#1664](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/1664) docs(positioning): adopt the 'Data Quality Control Plane' framing on the marketing page + docs site — [PR #2497](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2497): marketing page, docs landing, features tour and README; counts checked against the code |"," | ✅ | [#2395](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2395) Changelog fragments: one file per PR, assembled at release — [PR #2460](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2460): `changelog.d/<n>.<section>.md`, rendered into the docs page by a mkdocs hook, assembled by `scripts/changelog.py` at release, CI requires a fragment (or the `no-changelog` label) on user-facing PRs; CONTRIBUTING rule 43 |"," | ✅ | [#2440](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2440) feat(monitors): per-period metrics with yearly seasonality and seasonal periods on the anomaly monitor — **unplanned, net-new, taken on the maintainer's direction 2026-10-13** in a cycle scoped as no net-new features. ADR 0048 ([#2441](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2441)). Shipped: per-period metrics ([#2442](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2442)), history seeded from the table ([#2444](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2444)), yearly seasonality in scoring for the per-period metrics ([#2445](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2445)), the declared-calendar schema `seasonal_periods` + `check_seasonal_periods` ([#2447](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2447), migration `b94674780cb8`). the calendar service, admin API (`/admin/seasonal-periods`), attachments and declared-period scoring ([#2469](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2469)). detected periods, the promote action and their REST/MCP reads ([#2487](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2487)). Yearly on the whole-table metrics and in automatic coverage ([#2491](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2491)). The admin calendar, editor fields, trend expected value and run-detail explanation ([#2492](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/pull/2492)). Closed 2026-10-21; follow-ups [#2490](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2490), [#2498](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2498) in `v1.3 Backlog`. Filed: [#2443](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/2443) |"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/docs/progress.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"381b8d79-dcd0-4f92-9372-9d91eb50fce6","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cd602f2b-9d8e-4415-a26d-7deebe76a015","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
