{"parentUuid":"854a6ec3-f1ad-42cc-8a09-d4cf547f3f3e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEgjNpmd87HXTq1aj7qd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Current state for everything you asked about.\n\n**Merged this round**\n- **Week 2 is complete.** #2505 (Helm chart, #2388), #2501 (demo walkthrough, #2253) and #2497 (positioning, #1664) are all merged. Progress PR #2511 is open.\n- **#2508** fixed the dependency audits that had gone red on main.\n- I inspected the Helm branch myself, because its safety review couldn't run. I found nothing suspicious. CI's one download is `kubeconform`, and its checksum matches upstream.\n\n**CodeQL: 11 open alerts, all \"note\" severity**\n- **4 false positives, dismissed with reasons:**\n  - #204 `COMPARISON_KIND` is imported by other modules.\n  - #208 `llm_kinds` is a deliberate side-effect import.\n  - #209 and #210 are globals read through `global`, which CodeQL doesn't follow.\n- **7 cyclic-import alerts are a real cycle:** #206, #207 and #211–#215. The GCS adapter made `flatfile` and `sql_engines` import the registry lazily, and the registry imports both. PR #2510 moves the credential helpers into the registry, which ends the cycle. A static import check shows the cycle on main and none on the branch. The datasource, service and API tests pass (6,562), apart from #2358, a known failure that depends on test order. Its four review findings are fixed. CI is running and the alerts close when it merges.\n\n**Dependabot #50 and #51**\n\nBoth are the same critical `certifi` advisory: bundled emSign roots with compromised intermediate keys. #2508 fixed it at 2026.10.19, which is the only `certifi` pin in the repo. GitHub's dependency graph still lists the old version beside the new one for the same two files, a stale entry on GitHub's side, so the alerts haven't closed yet. I'll recheck them. Deployments get the fixed CA bundle only once images are rebuilt from main.\n\n**Accessibility: where we are**\n- **Automated floor:**\n  - Every route is scanned in both themes, including the new admin Calendar page. The test checking scan coverage against the router passes.\n  - The Calendar page has its own axe checks.\n  - There are 9 keyboard tests.\n  - The contrast token tests pass.\n  - None of this has regressed since the September track.\n- **Still open, all planned for Week 7:**\n  - #1672 keyboard and focus audit. The SQL editor has no accessibility options set, so Tab is trapped inside it unless the user knows Ctrl+M. The lineage graph has no keyboard path.\n  - #1673 screen-reader semantics. The codebase has exactly one live region, on the sign-in page, so run progress is never announced. No table has a caption. Landmarks exist only because the UI library's layout renders them.\n  - #2067 detail pages have generic titles.\n  - #2061 printing from the dark theme keeps dark colours.\n  - #2051 the scan can't tell when a page was only half loaded.\n- **Related open bugs:** #2064 (navigation never resets scroll) in Week 7, and #2068 (run detail not refetching) in Week 6.\n- **New charts:** the seasonal trend chart added in phase 6 has a table view, but it hasn't been checked with a screen reader.\n\nThe accessibility work is sizeable and is Week 7 scope. I'd start it once Weeks 4 and 5 are under way. Say if you want it pulled forward."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1006,"cache_read_input_tokens":588361,"output_tokens":1290,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":133},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1006,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1290,"cache_read_input_tokens":588361,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1006},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"058a5332-0fe5-40a9-9d9e-3505dfb1f7c0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEgjNNUtdfdxopvU9eFq","requestRef":"6cf38cd6-a668-423f-be8a-35262c9c184e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"14da77c6-1010-4089-8410-2e18def6546a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T03:38:51.908Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ/frontend","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
