rnal","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b9076997-3df7-4272-9b0d-6bc325cf1203","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"484bc160-77e2-42c2-96e8-bcdeeb96fa10","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F51jxXFdX8Tm2mVKWNXT1C","type":"tool_result","content":"   **4b. Automated accessibility floor — axe-core, ratcheted, not big-bang** ([#1670](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/1670), Theme-3 item 1): `serious`/`critical` axe-core violations are checked on every PR, in the existing jobs — no new required check. The Playwright lane (`frontend/e2e/a11y.spec.ts` + `frontend/e2e-otp/a11y.spec.ts` for the sign-in screen, `@axe-core/playwright`) scans **every route, once per theme** against the real seeded stack (dark surfaces are keyed `route:/…@dark`; the sign-in card is white in both themes, so it is scanned once) — a route added to `App.tsx` or `pages/admin/routes.tsx` is added to the spec in the same PR (enforced: `frontend/tests/a11y/scanCoverage.test.ts` parses the routers and fails on a declared path with no scan, and `tests/utils/pageTitle.test.ts` does the same for its document title), and each scan first waits for the page to finish loading (`frontend/scripts/a11y/settle.ts`), because a scan that lands mid-load sees fewer violations and the ratchet cannot tell; the Vitest lane (`frontend/tests/a11y/components.a11y.test.tsx`, `axe-core` run directly against jsdom — **not** the `vitest-axe` npm package, a single-maintainer fork last published over a year ago and never promoted past `0.1.0`, which fails the rule-40 supply-chain bar) covers the check editor, connection form, suite form, results table, and notification panel. Token values axe cannot see — SVG fills, `Progress` strokes, inline-coloured text it silently skips — are held to the WCAG ratios directly by `frontend/tests/a11y/tokens.test.ts`. Keyboard-only operation is its own real-browser spec, `frontend/e2e/keyboard.spec.ts` (skip link, focus following navigation, every click-to-open row reachable by a link) — jsdom has no focus order, so none of it can live in Vitest, and a new click-to-navigate row or card gets a case there. A clean scan is a floor, not a verdict: axe judges only what is rendered, so overlays, the custom widgets the keyboard spec does not reach yet (the SQL editor, the lineage graph, drawer/modal focus return) and what a screen reader actually announces still need a browser check (the accessibility tree, not the DOM). Both lanes diff against the committed baseline `frontend/a11y-baseline.json` (shared logic in `frontend/scripts/a11y/ratchet.ts`) and fail ONLY on a violation not already in it — fixing what the baseline records is tracked separately, never silently re-added to the baseline to make a red run green. Regenerate the baseline deliberately, never by hand-editing the JSON, with `pnpm a11y:baseline` (needs the same CI-equivalent stack as `pnpm e2e` + `pnpm e2e:otp`; the otp phase needs no manual env — the script itself sets `E2E_OTP=1`) when a change to rendered markup is intentional — explain why in the PR.\n43. **Changelog entries are fragments, assembled at release.** A PR never edits the Unreleased part of `docs/site/reference/changelog.md`; it adds `changelog.d/<issue>.<section>.md` (`<issue>-<n>` for a second entry; section one of `breaking | security | added | changed | fixed`; body = the bullet's\n\n---","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"73dcca7e-24cf-4dc7-b2af-4adf3600034e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T03:58:03.424Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"   **4b. Automated accessibility floor — axe-core, ratcheted, not big-bang** ([#1670](https://github.com/TheurgicDuke771/DataQ/issues/1670), Theme-3 item 1): `serious`/`critical` axe-core violations are checked on every PR, in the existing jobs — no new required check. The Playwright lane (`frontend/e2e/a11y.spec.ts` + `frontend/e2e-otp/a11y.spec.ts` for the sign-in screen, `@axe-core/playwright`) scans **every route, once per theme** against the real seeded stack (dark surfaces are keyed `route:/…@dark`; the sign-in card is white in both themes, so it is scanned once) — a route added to `App.tsx` or `pages/admin/routes.tsx` is added to the spec in the same PR (enforced: `frontend/tests/a11y/scanCoverage.test.ts` parses the routers and fails on a declared path with no scan, and `tests/utils/pageTitle.test.ts` does the same for its document title), and each scan first waits for the page to finish loading (`frontend/scripts/a11y/settle.ts`), because a scan that lands mid-load sees fewer violations and the ratchet cannot tell; the Vitest lane (`frontend/tests/a11y/components.a11y.test.tsx`, `axe-core` run directly against jsdom — **not** the `vitest-axe` npm package, a single-maintainer fork last published over a year ago and never promoted past `0.1.0`, which fails the rule-40 supply-chain bar) covers the check editor, connection form, suite form, results table, and notification panel. Token values axe cannot see — SVG fills, `Progress` strokes, inline-coloured text it silently skips — are held to the WCAG ratios directly by `frontend/tests/a11y/tokens.test.ts`. Keyboard-only operation is its own real-browser spec, `frontend/e2e/keyboard.spec.ts` (skip link, focus following navigation, every click-to-open row reachable by a link) — jsdom has no focus order, so none of it can live in Vitest, and a new click-to-navigate row or card gets a case there. A clean scan is a floor, not a verdict: axe judges only what is rendered, so overlays, the custom widgets the keyboard spec does not reach yet (the SQL editor, the lineage graph, drawer/modal focus return) and what a screen reader actually announces still need a browser check (the accessibility tree, not the DOM). Both lanes diff against the committed baseline `frontend/a11y-baseline.json` (shared logic in `frontend/scripts/a11y/ratchet.ts`) and fail ONLY on a violation not already in it — fixing what the baseline records is tracked separately, never silently re-added to the baseline to make a red run green. Regenerate the baseline deliberately, never by hand-editing the JSON, with `pnpm a11y:baseline` (needs the same CI-equivalent stack as `pnpm e2e` + `pnpm e2e:otp`; the otp phase needs no manual env — the script itself sets `E2E_OTP=1`) when a change to rendered markup is intentional — explain why in the PR.\n43. **Changelog entries are fragments, assembled at release.** A PR never edits the Unreleased part of `docs/site/reference/changelog.md`; it adds `changelog.d/<issue>.<section>.md` (`<issue>-<n>` for a second entry; section one of `breaking | security | added | changed | fixed`; body = the bullet's\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b10d1fd1-4bd1-4760-ad04-80467aab1d31","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","root":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"TheurgicDuke771/DataQ","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b9076997-3df7-4272-9b0d-6bc325cf1203","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main"}
