{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"641b53ca-47b3-45aa-9ab6-6db8524d561d","hash":"5cb787b1429b169416901226f0412b400bc635b39fbf122f58f04efae392e995","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mmi65vXe7q9hvNvJUC4jk4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && git checkout -q -b docs/new-code-meets-standards origin/main && /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\nc=pathlib.Path(\"CONTRIBUTING.md\"); t=c.read_text().split(\"\\n\")\ni=next(k for k,l in enumerate(t) if l.startswith(\"43. \"))\nrule = (\"44. **New code meets the standards already in force; a known gap is not a licence to widen it.** \"\n\"Open debt (the Week-7 accessibility audits #1672/#1673, any filed backlog item) is fixed on its own schedule, but a PR \"\n\"adds nothing to it. For UI, beyond rule 4b's automated floor: every new control is reachable and operable by keyboard, \"\n\"a dialog or drawer takes focus on open and returns it on close, every control and icon button has an accessible name, \"\n\"status that changes without navigation (a run, a save, an async result) is announced through a live region, a chart has \"\n\"a text or table alternative, colours come from the theme tokens in both themes, a new click-to-navigate row gets a \"\n\"`keyboard.spec.ts` case, and the change is checked in the browser's accessibility tree rather than the DOM. \"\n\"For the other surfaces, the existing bars apply to new code without exception: MCP tools state their blind spots \"\n\"(the `mcp-honesty-reviewer` agent on any change to `backend/app/mcp/server.py`), migrations follow rules 30–31 \"\n\"(the `migration-safety` agent), dependencies pass rule 40's licence gate, published docs follow rule 41, values \"\n\"crossing a driver boundary are tested in the shape the driver returns (the `driver-boundary-guard` agent), \"\n\"and secrets and PII follow sections E and H. \"\n\"Where a standard cannot be met in the PR, the PR says which and links the filed issue.\")\nt.insert(i+1, rule)\nc.write_text(\"\\n\".join(t))\np=pathlib.Path(\".github/pull_request_template.md\"); s=p.read_text()\nanchor=\"- [ ] **Security implications considered** (auth, input validation, secret handling, PII in logs)\\n\"\nadd=anchor+\"\"\"\n## Standards for new code (CONTRIBUTING rule 44)\n\n<!-- Tick what applies; write N/A beside a group that does not. A standard the PR cannot meet is named here with its filed issue. -->\n- [ ] **UI a11y:** new controls work by keyboard; dialogs and drawers take and return focus; every control has an accessible name; async status is announced (live region); charts have a text or table alternative; theme tokens only, both themes; new routes scanned (rule 4b) and new click-to-navigate rows have a `keyboard.spec.ts` case; checked in the accessibility tree\n- [ ] **MCP:** `mcp-honesty-reviewer` run on any `backend/app/mcp/server.py` change; sibling docstrings re-read\n- [ ] **Migrations:** `migration-safety` run; single alembic head after merging `main`\n- [ ] **Dependencies:** pinned in the single source of truth; licence gate passes\n- [ ] **Driver boundary:** values from a driver/SDK tested in the shape it returns (`driver-boundary-guard`)\n- [ ] **Published docs:** no ticket or internal-doc references; counts checked against the code\n\"\"\"\nassert anchor in s; p.write_text(s.replace(anchor,add,1))\nm=pathlib.Path(\"CLAUDE.md\"); u=m.read_text()\nu=u.replace(\"Full list (42 rules across 8 categories)\",\"Full list (44 rules across 8 categories)\").replace(\"full 42-rule working agreements\",\"full 44-rule working agreements\").replace(\"Working agreements (full 42-rule list)\",\"Working agreements (full 44-rule list)\")\nm.write_text(u)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | cat; for s in scripts/check-docs-*.py; do /opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/dataq/bin/python $s >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo \"FAIL $s\"; done; echo guards-done","description":"Add CONTRIBUTING rule 44, the PR-template standards section, and fix the rule count"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
