{"parentUuid":"840203a9-24e9-4386-8fba-ce206030492b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEiJpGFw2P9qgQ2TstQk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014sobWydp2J19CTXDg4QqgD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git branch --show-current && git add -A CONTRIBUTING.md CLAUDE.md .github/pull_request_template.md && git commit -q -m \"docs(contributing): rule 44 — new code meets the standards already in force\n\nOpen debt (the Week-7 a11y audits, filed backlog items) is fixed on its own\nschedule, but a PR adds nothing to it. The rule spells out what that means for\nnew UI beyond rule 4b's automated floor, and names the existing review agents\nfor MCP, migrations, licences, docs and driver-boundary values. The PR template\ngets a matching checklist. CLAUDE.md's rule count was stale (42) and is now 44.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"failed|error\"; git push -q -u origin docs/new-code-meets-standards 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error|rejected\"; gh pr create --title \"docs(contributing): rule 44 — new code meets the standards already in force\" --body \"Maintainer direction (2026-10-21): accessibility stays a Week-7 track, but every change shipped before then must comply with the standards already in force, accessibility included.\n\n- **CONTRIBUTING rule 44.** A known gap is not a licence to widen it. For UI it lists what rule 4b's automated floor cannot see: keyboard operation, dialog focus in and out, accessible names, live regions for async status, chart text alternatives, theme tokens in both themes, \\`keyboard.spec.ts\\` cases for new click-to-navigate rows, and a check in the accessibility tree. It names the existing review agents for MCP, migrations, licences, published docs and driver-boundary values. A standard a PR cannot meet is named in the PR with its filed issue.\n- **PR template.** A short checklist for the same groups.\n- **CLAUDE.md.** The rule count said 42; it is 44.\n\n- N/A — process docs, no user-facing change (\\`no-changelog\\`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" --label \"no-changelog,documentation\" --milestone \"v1.3 Week 3 — datasources, deploy targets & auth\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git checkout -q main","description":"Commit and open the rule-44 PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":600063,"output_tokens":953,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":46},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":468,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":600063,"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":468},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014sobWydp2J19CTXDg4QqgD":{"command":"cd /Users/arijit/Coding/Python/DataQ && git branch --show-current && git add -A CONTRIBUTING.md CLAUDE.md .github/pull_request_template.md && git commit -q -m \"docs(contributing): rule 44 — new code meets the standards already in force\n\nOpen debt (the Week-7 a11y audits, filed backlog items) is fixed on its own\nschedule, but a PR adds nothing to it. The rule spells out what that means for\nnew UI beyond rule 4b's automated floor, and names the existing review agents\nfor MCP, migrations, licences, docs and driver-boundary values. The PR template\ngets a matching checklist. CLAUDE.md's rule count was stale (42) and is now 44.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"failed|error\"; git push -q -u origin docs/new-code-meets-standa